6. Full Replication Cost Specification
6.1 Replication Cost Schema
The replication cost schema defines the structure of a replication cost estimate deposit.

It has the following fields:

estimate_id. A string. Required.

estimate_name. A string. Required.

study_reference. A string. Required.

study_description. A string. Required.

method. An object. Required. It contains design, sample_size, population, instruments, duration_months, and number_of_sites.

cost_categories. An array of cost category objects. Required.

total_cost. An object. Required. It contains value, currency, and year.

cost_uncertainty. An object. Required. It contains lower and upper.

cost_drivers. An array of cost driver objects. Required.

cost_assumptions. An array of assumption objects. Required.

cost_per_participant. An object. Optional. It contains value and currency.

cost_per_site. An object. Optional. It contains value and currency.

cost_per_month. An object. Optional. It contains value and currency.

original_study_cost. An object. Optional. It contains value, currency, year, and source.

inflation_adjustment. An object. Optional. It contains base_year, target_year, and adjustment_factor.

funding_sources. An array of funding source objects. Optional.

funding_gap. An object. Optional. It contains value and currency.

related_estimates. An array of estimate relations. Optional.

provenance. An object. Required.

work_reference. A string. Optional.

replication_tracker_reference. A string. Optional.

instrument_reference. A string. Optional.

keywords. An array of strings. Optional.

notes. A string. Optional.

moderation_status. An enum. The values are pending, approved, rejected.

version. An integer.

supersedes. A string. Optional.

superseded_by. A string. Optional.

The method object has:

design. An enum. The values are randomized_controlled_trial, cohort, case_control, cross_sectional, longitudinal, experimental, observational, simulation, survey, other.

sample_size. An integer.

population. A string.

instruments. An array of strings.

duration_months. An integer.

number_of_sites. An integer.

Each cost category object has:

category_id. A string.

category_name. An enum. The values are personnel, equipment, materials, travel, participant_compensation, publication, overhead, other.

category_description. A string.

category_cost. An object. It contains value and currency.

percentage_of_total. A number. Optional.

notes. A string. Optional.

Each cost driver object has:

driver_id. A string.

driver_description. A string.

driver_type. An enum. The values are sample_size, duration, number_of_sites, instrument_cost, participant_compensation, personnel_seniority, travel_distance, regulatory_requirements, other.

driver_impact. An object. It contains value and currency.

notes. A string. Optional.

Each assumption object has:

assumption_id. A string.

assumption_description. A string.

assumption_type. An enum. The values are personnel_rate, instrument_rate, participant_rate, overhead_rate, inflation_rate, other.

assumption_value. An object. It contains value and units.

notes. A string. Optional.

Each funding source object has:

source_id. A string.

source_name. A string.

source_type. An enum. The values are government, industry, non_profit, university, internal, other.

source_amount. An object. It contains value and currency.

source_conditions. A string. Optional.

Each estimate relation has:

relation_id. A string.

related_estimate_id. A string.

relation_type. An enum. The values are same_study, same_method, alternative, complement, related, independent.

relation_note. A string. Optional.

