7. Core Logic as Executable Pseudocode
7.1 Create Replication Cost Estimate
function createReplicationCost(estimate, files, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "depositor"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Validate the estimate against the schema. If invalid, return an error with the details.

Step 3. If the work reference is present, look it up. If null, flag it as unresolved.

Step 4. If the replication tracker reference is present, look it up. If null, flag it as unresolved.

Step 5. If the instrument reference is present, look it up. If null, flag it as unresolved.

Step 6. Generate an estimate ID. Set the fields: version 1, moderation_status pending, deposit_date now, depositor_id from auth, depositor_affiliation from auth, provenance from provenance.

Step 7. Insert the replication cost.

Step 8. Insert the cost categories, the cost drivers, the assumptions, the funding sources, and the estimate relations.

Step 9. Insert the work link, the replication tracker link, and the instrument link if present.

Step 10. Insert the provenance.

Step 11. Insert the moderation record.

Step 12. Insert the audit log entry.

Step 13. Return the estimate_id and the status created.

7.2 Read Replication Cost Estimate
function readReplicationCost(estimateId, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the estimate. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Read the cost categories, the cost drivers, the assumptions, the funding sources, the relations, the links, the provenance, and the moderation.

Step 4. Reconstruct the deposit.

Step 5. Insert the audit log entry.

Step 6. Return the deposit.

7.3 Update Replication Cost Estimate
function updateReplicationCost(estimateId, estimate, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "depositor"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the existing estimate. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Validate the new estimate.

Step 4. Increment the version. Update the supersedes and superseded_by fields.

Step 5. Insert a provenance record with operation update.

Step 6. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 7. Return the estimate_id, the version, and the status updated.

7.4 Delete Replication Cost Estimate
function deleteReplicationCost(estimateId, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "admin"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the existing estimate. If null, return an error.

Step 3. If soft delete, mark as deleted. Otherwise, remove.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the estimate_id and the status deleted.

7.5 Compute Cost
function computeCost(estimateId, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the estimate. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Read the cost categories, the cost drivers, and the assumptions.

Step 4. Sum the cost categories to get the total cost.

Step 5. Apply the assumptions: personnel rate, instrument rate, participant rate, overhead rate, inflation rate.

Step 6. Compute the uncertainty: the lower and upper bounds based on the assumptions.

Step 7. Compute the cost per participant, the cost per site, and the cost per month.

Step 8. Compute the inflation adjustment if an original study cost is present.

Step 9. Compute the funding gap if funding sources are present.

Step 10. Update the estimate's total_cost, cost_uncertainty, cost_per_participant, cost_per_site, cost_per_month, inflation_adjustment, and funding_gap fields.

Step 11. Insert the audit log entry.

Step 12. Return the estimate.

