12. Validation Engine Design
The system validates the following.

Validation 1. Estimate validity. Every estimate is validated against the schema.

Validation 2. Referential integrity.

Validation 3. Version chain acyclicity.

Validation 4. Work resolution.

Validation 5. Replication tracker record resolution.

Validation 6. Instrument resolution.

Validation 7. Provenance completeness.

Validation 8. Audit completeness.

Validation 9. Moderation completeness.

Validation 10. Cost consistency. The cost categories must sum to the total.

Validation 11. Uncertainty consistency. The lower and upper bounds must be consistent with the total.

Validation 12. Per-unit consistency. The cost per participant, per site, and per month must be consistent with the total and the method.

Validation 13. Inflation consistency. The inflation adjustment must be consistent with the original study cost and the base and target years.

Validation 14. Funding gap consistency. The funding gap must be consistent with the total and the funding sources.

